win32u: GetWindowPlacement/SetWindowPlacement use workspace coordinates for top-level windows, as on Windows (NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE)

His words for this family: "When I used meta shift left to move it to the main monitor it appeared off screen and the wrong scale."
Seen (lab mcb3/wplace, Media Composer 2025 in his signed-in copy, his layout: 175% screen with a 32 px top panel + 100% screen):
after New Project MC opens its main window maximized; restored with MC's own title-bar button, its normal rect came back 56 px
lower than before it was maximized, (1,56)-(3840,2160) -> (1,112)-(3840,2216): 56 px past the bottom of the 175% monitor,
whose work area starts 56 px (32 logical) down.

Mechanism (SOLID for Wine's side, probe wpl.exe): Wine's NtUserGetWindowPlacement returned rcNormalPosition in SCREEN
coordinates and NtUserSetWindowPlacement took it as screen coordinates, for every window. Windows (WINDOWPLACEMENT): "If the
window is a top-level window that does not have the WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW window style, then the coordinates represented by the
following members are in workspace coordinates: ptMinPosition, ptMaxPosition, and rcNormalPosition. Otherwise, these members
are in screen coordinates." Workspace coordinates are screen coordinates less the offset of the monitor's work area from the
monitor's corner -- the offset Qt applies (qwindowswindow.cpp windowPlacementOffset = availableGeometry().topLeft() -
geometry().topLeft()) when it reads a minimized window's rect and when it gives SetWindowPlacement the normal rect of a
maximized or minimized window. An application that converts as on Windows moves the window by the work-area offset on each
round trip under Wine; with the panel at the bottom (Windows' default) the offset is 0, so it never shows there, and Wine's own
test_window_placement (rcNormalPosition compared with the screen rect) passes on Windows test machines without testing this.

Fix: at the API boundary only, NtUserGetWindowPlacement maps rcNormalPosition from screen to workspace coordinates and
NtUserSetWindowPlacement maps it back, for a top-level (desktop child), non-WS_CHILD window without WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW, by the
work-area offset of the monitor the rect is on, in the caller's dpi. Win32u's own callers (GetInternalWindowPos, the
minimize/maximize/restore path, MonitorFromWindow for a minimized window) keep screen coordinates through the new
get_window_placement(). The first 64 mappings per process are logged ("neutron-wplace: ..."), in both arms.

Not covered: ptMinPosition and ptMaxPosition stay in screen coordinates (Windows documents them as workspace too; no application
seen that depends on it, and leaving both Get and Set alone keeps a round trip exact). Get/SetInternalWindowPos (undocumented)
stay screen. The monitor is chosen from the rect as given (screen rect for Get, workspace rect for Set); a rect that straddles a
monitor edge within the work-area offset may pick the neighbour's offset. No Windows probe: his Windows box has one monitor with
the taskbar at the bottom (work area at its corner), where both rules give the same numbers.
Applies after hdpi-pm-move-mfw (its sysparams.c hunk is the context of this patch's MonitorFromWindow change).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE=0.

Lab evidence (lab wplace, desk mirroring his layout: V0 3840x2160@1.75 + 32 px top panel, V1 1920x1080@1 at 2195,94 + 32 px top panel;
runtime 11.10-214wp5 = 214 + hdpi-pm-move-mfw + hdpi-fs-client + ncbutton-appframe v3 + frame-fit v2 + this):
- probe wpl.exe on the 100% monitor (work area 32 px down): fix pwf1,pwf2 = documented rule at every step (Get = screen - 32,
  Set(x,y) -> window at y+32, Set while maximized + restore -> +32), WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW unchanged; kill pwk1,pwk2 = 214 (screen).
- Media Composer (his signed-in copy, main's OK, unpinned): MC reads GetWindowPlacement and calls SetWindowPlacement with that
  rect + 56 (the work-area offset Qt knows): kill x3 Get (1,56) -> Set (1,112); fix d1/f4/f5 Get (1,0) -> Set (1,56) -> (1,112).
  So this patch does NOT change MC's restored rect (both arms (1,112)); MC's drift is its own arithmetic (INFERRED: the same on
  Windows with a work area 56 px down). Not a non-client height: Wine's WS_OVERLAPPEDWINDOW top inset at 168 dpi is 50.
- Every MC arm's Select Project dialog: select:ok (check3), both arms.
Rebased onto 227.1 (b3) by lab lr61e on 11-25 for the 227.1pc lab runtime: the published patch applies to the 227.1 tree with
offsets and fuzz 1 in sysparams.c (MonitorFromWindow's iconic line, checked by hand); this diff (diff -u of the 227.1 files)
applies cleanly. Code unchanged from a29.

In 11.10-231.1 (hotfix line): carried as 227a71 = main's 227a29 (wplwork) rebased onto the 227.1/227.2 tree by lab lr61e
(+/- lines identical to a29). It is in 231.1 because the placement-bounds patch (227a72) works in workspace coordinates.
Round 54 (owner's Windows box, taskbar at the bottom: work area at the monitor's corner, offset 0) cannot tell screen from
workspace coordinates; the rule here is the documented one. Known gap (lr61e, SOLID from the numbers): our work area puts a
BOTTOM panel's inset at the TOP ((0,57)-(3840,2160) on a 150 % monitor with a 38 px bottom panel), so on such a desktop the
offset is 57 where Windows has 0: a normal rect that Lightroom saved under 227/227.2/231 (screen coordinates) comes back 57 px
lower once, e.g. LrC's own (30,86)-(3810,2130) -> (30,143)-(3810,2187), 27 px past the bottom. Top-panel desktops (KDE/GNOME
with the panel at the top) get the right offset. Kill switch NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE=0.

--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -3945,10 +3945,88 @@
     return pt.x == -1 && pt.y == -1;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON placement-workspace: kill switch NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE=0 (see placement_map_workspace). */
+static BOOL neutron_placement_workspace(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE" );
+        on = !e || e[0] != '0';
+        if (!on) ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_PLACEMENT_WORKSPACE = 0 (environment)\n" );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
+/* NEUTRON placement-workspace (11-17, lab wplace; his words for the family: "When I used meta shift left to move it to the
+ * main monitor it appeared off screen and the wrong scale"). Media Composer's main window, maximized after New Project and
+ * restored with its own title-bar button, came back 56 px lower than before it was maximized: (1,56)-(3840,2160) became
+ * (1,112)-(3840,2216) on the 175% screen, whose work area starts 56 px down (a 32 px top panel), so the restored window ran
+ * 56 px past the bottom of its monitor. Windows (WINDOWPLACEMENT): "If the window is a top-level window that does not have
+ * the WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW window style, then the coordinates represented by ptMinPosition, ptMaxPosition and rcNormalPosition
+ * are in workspace coordinates" -- relative to the work area, i.e. a screen rect less the offset of its monitor's work area
+ * from the monitor's corner (Qt: windowPlacementOffset = availableGeometry().topLeft() - geometry().topLeft(), which it
+ * adds to what GetWindowPlacement returns and takes off what it gives SetWindowPlacement). Wine's GetWindowPlacement and
+ * SetWindowPlacement used SCREEN coordinates for every window, so an application that converts as on Windows moved the
+ * window down (or up) by the work-area offset on every round trip; with a panel at the bottom only, both are equal, which is
+ * why Wine's own tests (test_window_placement compares rcNormalPosition with the screen rect) pass on Windows test machines.
+ * Here, at the API boundary only (NtUserGetWindowPlacement / NtUserSetWindowPlacement), rcNormalPosition of a top-level,
+ * non-tool window is mapped between screen and workspace coordinates by the work-area offset of the monitor the rect is on,
+ * in the caller's dpi. Win32u's own callers keep screen coordinates (get_window_placement). Not mapped: ptMinPosition and
+ * ptMaxPosition (no application seen that depends on them; left as Wine had them, so a Get/Set round trip stays exact),
+ * NtUserGetInternalWindowPos / NtUserSetInternalWindowPos (undocumented; screen as before). */
+static BOOL placement_uses_workspace( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    if (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CHILD) return FALSE;
+    if (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) return FALSE;
+    return NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT ) == get_desktop_window();
+}
+
+/* to_workspace TRUE: screen -> workspace (GetWindowPlacement); FALSE: workspace -> screen (SetWindowPlacement) */
+static void placement_map_workspace( HWND hwnd, RECT *rect, BOOL to_workspace )
+{
+    static LONG logged;
+    static HWND last_hwnd;
+    static RECT last_rect;
+    MONITORINFO info;
+    RECT before = *rect;
+    int dx, dy;
+    BOOL on;
+
+    if (!placement_uses_workspace( hwnd )) return;
+    info = monitor_info_from_rect( *rect, get_thread_dpi() );
+    dx = info.rcWork.left - info.rcMonitor.left;
+    dy = info.rcWork.top - info.rcMonitor.top;
+    if (!dx && !dy) return;
+    on = neutron_placement_workspace();
+    if (on)
+    {
+        if (to_workspace) OffsetRect( rect, -dx, -dy );
+        else OffsetRect( rect, dx, dy );
+    }
+    /* a GetWindowPlacement is logged when its answer changed (applications poll it), every SetWindowPlacement */
+    if (!to_workspace || hwnd != last_hwnd || !EqualRect( &before, &last_rect ))
+    {
+        if (to_workspace)
+        {
+            last_hwnd = hwnd;
+            last_rect = before;
+        }
+        if (InterlockedIncrement( &logged ) <= 400)
+        ERR( "neutron-wplace: %s hwnd=%p normal %s %s %s (work area of monitor %s starts %d,%d in)\n",
+             to_workspace ? "GetWindowPlacement" : "SetWindowPlacement", hwnd, wine_dbgstr_rect(&before),
+             on ? (to_workspace ? "-> workspace" : "-> screen") : "KILL SWITCH: left as", wine_dbgstr_rect(rect),
+             wine_dbgstr_rect(&info.rcMonitor), dx, dy );
+    }
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
- *           NtUserGetWindowPlacement (win32u.@)
+ *           get_window_placement
+ *
+ * NEUTRON placement-workspace: NtUserGetWindowPlacement's former body; rcNormalPosition in SCREEN coordinates (win32u's
+ * own callers). The exported call maps it to workspace coordinates.
  */
-BOOL WINAPI NtUserGetWindowPlacement( HWND hwnd, WINDOWPLACEMENT *placement )
+BOOL get_window_placement( HWND hwnd, WINDOWPLACEMENT *placement )
 {
     WND *win = get_win_ptr( hwnd );
     UINT win_dpi;
@@ -4034,6 +4112,17 @@
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           NtUserGetWindowPlacement (win32u.@)
+ */
+BOOL WINAPI NtUserGetWindowPlacement( HWND hwnd, WINDOWPLACEMENT *placement )
+{
+    if (!get_window_placement( hwnd, placement )) return FALSE;
+    /* NEUTRON placement-workspace: rcNormalPosition in workspace coordinates, as on Windows */
+    if (hwnd && !is_desktop_window( hwnd )) placement_map_workspace( hwnd, &placement->rcNormalPosition, TRUE );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
 /* make sure the specified rect is visible on screen */
 static void make_rect_onscreen( RECT *rect )
 {
@@ -4070,7 +4159,7 @@
     WINDOWPLACEMENT placement;
 
     placement.length = sizeof(placement);
-    if (!NtUserGetWindowPlacement( hwnd, &placement )) return 0;
+    if (!get_window_placement( hwnd, &placement )) return 0;
     if (rect) *rect = placement.rcNormalPosition;
     if (pt) *pt = placement.ptMinPosition;
     return placement.showCmd;
@@ -4179,6 +4268,14 @@
         return FALSE;
     }
     if (wpl->flags & WPF_SETMINPOSITION) flags |= PLACE_MIN;
+    /* NEUTRON placement-workspace: the application gives rcNormalPosition in workspace coordinates, as on Windows */
+    if (hwnd && !is_desktop_window( hwnd ))
+    {
+        WINDOWPLACEMENT wp = *wpl;
+
+        placement_map_workspace( hwnd, &wp.rcNormalPosition, FALSE );
+        return set_window_placement( hwnd, &wp, flags );
+    }
     return set_window_placement( hwnd, wpl, flags );
 }
 
@@ -5962,7 +6059,7 @@
     TRACE( "%p %u\n", hwnd, cmd );
 
     wpl.length = sizeof(wpl);
-    NtUserGetWindowPlacement( hwnd, &wpl );
+    get_window_placement( hwnd, &wpl );
 
     if (call_hooks( WH_CBT, HCBT_MINMAX, (WPARAM)hwnd, cmd, 0 ))
         return SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOMOVE;
--- a/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
@@ -343,6 +343,7 @@
 extern LONG_PTR set_window_long( HWND hwnd, INT offset, UINT size, LONG_PTR newval,
                                  BOOL ansi );
 extern void set_window_normal_placement( HWND hwnd, RECT rect );
+extern BOOL get_window_placement( HWND hwnd, WINDOWPLACEMENT *placement ); /* NEUTRON placement-workspace: screen coords */
 extern BOOL set_window_pos( WINDOWPOS *winpos, int parent_x, int parent_y );
 extern UINT set_window_style_bits( HWND hwnd, UINT set_bits, UINT clear_bits );
 extern void update_window_state( HWND hwnd );
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5047,7 +5047,7 @@
     if ((override = get_window_monitor_override( hwnd ))) return override;
 
     wp.length = sizeof(wp);
-    if (is_iconic( hwnd ) && NtUserGetWindowPlacement( hwnd, &wp ))
+    if (is_iconic( hwnd ) && get_window_placement( hwnd, &wp ))
         return monitor_from_rect( &wp.rcNormalPosition, flags, dpi );
 
     if (get_window_rect( hwnd, &rect, dpi ))
